@style(../styles/IDocDemo.style)
@title(Variables and expressions)

Set a value once and print it anywhere; evaluate expressions; read values from a profile.

@section(Values)

@subsection(@@set)

Set a variable — a fixed value or an expression over other variables.

@set(f = factorial(5))

@set(V=12)

@set(half=V/2)

@@let is the same as @@set: @let(w=7) w is @var(w).

@subsection(@@var)

Print a variable's value.

@@val is the same as @@var: @val(w)

@subsection(@@var_noc)

Print a variable's value, no check.

@var_noc(acknowledge)

@subsection(@@exp)

Evaluate an expression inline and print the result.

@exp(V/R)

@@eval is the same as @@exp: @eval(2+3)

@subsection(@@print)

Print name = value for a variable (or just the value for an expression).

@print(V)

@section(Number formats)

@subsection(@@bin)

Print a value in BINARY.

@bin(m)
@bin4(m)

@subsection(@@hex)

Print a value in HEX; a width in the name zero-pads it (hex2(n) → 0A).

@hex(n)
@hex2(n)

@subsection(@@oct)

Print a value in OCTAL; a width in the name zero-pads it.

@oct(x)
@oct3(x)

@subsection(@@factorial)

n!

@factorial(20)

@factorial(n)

@section(Profiles and parameters)

@subsection(@@getvar)

Read a value from a PROFILE — a key=value file of the things that are true about you rather than about the document (your name, your school, this year and semester).

@getvar(instructor, PROFILE)

@getvar(adinstructor[@var(courseid)], PROFILE)
@inherits(@getvar(school, PROFILE))

@subsection(@@profile)

Name the profile a bare getvar(key) reads from.

@profile(Teaching)

@subsection(@@param)

A parameter passed into an included document or stylesheet, readable as a variable.

@param(topic)
@style(../styles/IDocDemo.style, topic="DC")
